{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cf9hFiQLwFuJagTbYotUn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Clean working tree, and every touched path matches a claim. The work for item #151 is committed on `attavo/151-invocation-marker`:\n\n- **Invocation markers**: `attavo drive` now commits and pushes a `<stage>-NN.started` marker (host, pid, sha, product_version) before running build/verify, so a dead or hung invocation leaves a fact on the branch.\n- **Doctor's fifth proof** (`no-invocation-lacks-record`): fails naming a marker whose record never arrived (dead pid, no `[drive].stall_after_s` → explicit refusal), holds once the record lands or the invocation is confirmed still running.\n- **`attavo drive --recover [N]`**: retires every pending marker for an item — `died` when the pid is gone, `hung` when it outlives `stall_after_s` with no newer event (and terminates it) — writing a `failed` record with provenance `product`, committed/pushed as the driver identity.\n- **Schema/config**: `died`/`hung` added to both stage schemas' `stop.class` enums and `STOP_CLASSES`; `[drive].stall_after_s` added to the manifest schema and `attavo.toml` (1800s).\n- **Ledger**: a marker's own commit classifies as `record`/product act, not `transport`.\n- Added test coverage in `tests/test_doctor.py`, `tests/test_drive.py`, `tests/test_ledger.py`; fixed a pre-existing `test_drive.py` assertion whose merge-commit expectation shifted now that the marker's push meets a divergent remote first.\n\nAll three spec criteria pass, and the full suite is green (354 passed) apart from two pre-existing, unrelated `test_adapters.py` failures confirmed present on the unmodified baseline (a model-derivation bug outside this item's claims)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":580,"cache_read_input_tokens":259034,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_i